Package: aDIFic
Title: Anchor-Free DIF Inference with Item Covariates in Moderated
    Nonlinear Factor Analysis
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Sanford R.", "Student", , "sanford.r.student@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7419-2437"))
Description: Estimation and inference for differential item functioning
    (DIF) of binary items in a two-parameter logistic moderated nonlinear
    factor analysis with item covariates, without anchor items. Item
    difficulty DIF with respect to any number of continuous or categorical
    person covariates is decomposed into a part explained by item
    covariates and item-specific residual DIF, identified by a sparsity
    assumption that generalizes the minimal-L1 condition of Chen et al.
    (2023) <doi:10.1007/s11336-023-09930-9>. Inference uses a
    threshold-centered parametric bootstrap, with Benjamini-Hochberg
    flags for residual DIF and diagnostics for the identifying assumption.
